   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=TEST_SIZE, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# StandardScaler is fitted ONLY on training data — no test data is seen during fitting.\n",
    "# This prevents data leakage; the same scaler parameters are then applied to the test set.\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "Xtr_sc = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "Xte_sc = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {len(y_train)}, Test: {len(y_test)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "07ddc4be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Experiments\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.1 Select best alpha via cross-validation (on training data only — never on the test set)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hyperparameter selection must not use the test set; otherwise, the reported test performance would\n",
    "reflect the specific test split rather than true generalization. We use:\n",
    "- **Ridge:** `RidgeCV(cv=None)` — efficient leave-one-out via the SVD decomposition, equivalent to\n",
    "  explicit 5-fold but ~7× faster for Ridge.\n",
    "- **Lasso:** `LassoCV` with explicit 5-fold CV on 100 alpha values on a log scale."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "3826390e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-29T15:21:29.800969Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-29T15:21:29.800778Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-29T15:21:45.808556Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-29T15:21:45.807204Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Best Ridge alpha: 0.0225\n",
      "Best Lasso alpha: 20.5651\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ridgecv = RidgeCV(alphas=np.logspace(-2, 5, 200), cv=None, scoring=\"r2\")  # cv=None -> efficient closed-form LOO\n",
    "ridgecv.fit(Xtr_sc, y_train)\n",
    "best_alpha_ridge = ridgecv.alpha_\n",
    "\n",
    "lassocv = LassoCV(alphas=np.logspace(0, 5, 100), cv=CV_FOLDS, max_iter=5000, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "lassocv.fit(Xtr_sc, y_train)\n",
    "best_alpha_lasso = lassocv.alpha_\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Best Ridge alpha: {best_alpha_ridge:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best Lasso alpha: {best_alpha_lasso:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
